etadata":{}}]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["# Interpretation of Surveillance Monitoring Chart\n","\n","The surveillance monitoring chart illustrates the relationship between observed outbreak activity and dynamically calculated statistical thresholds.\n","\n","Several important patterns are evident:\n","\n","- The rolling mean adapts to changing outbreak conditions throughout the study period.\n","- Statistical warning and alert thresholds increase during periods of elevated transmission and decrease during periods of lower transmission.\n","- The seven-day moving average exceeded warning and alert thresholds during multiple periods, indicating episodes of unusually high outbreak activity.\n","- The most intense outbreak activity occurred between July and August 2020, where the moving-average series approached or exceeded the upper alert threshold.\n","- Following the peak period, the surveillance indicators gradually declined, reflecting reduced transmission activity.\n","\n","The adaptive behavior of the thresholds demonstrates the usefulness of rolling surveillance methods for monitoring changing disease conditions."],"metadata":{"id":"o06OpZJ2up7z"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["## Daily Risk Classification Timeline\n","\n","The following figure shows the evolution of surveillance risk levels throughout the study period."],"metadata":{"id":"cS5fvzxDuJQd"}},{"cell_type":"code","source":["risk_colors = {\n","    \"Low\": \"green\",\n","    \"Moderate\": \"gold\",\n","    \"High\": \"orange\",\n","    \"Critical\": \"red\"\n","}\n","\n","plt.figure(figsize=(16,8))\n","\n","for level in risk_colors:\n","\n","    subset = ghana[\n","        ghana[\"risk_level\"] == level\n","    ]\n","\n","    plt.scatter(\n","        subset[\"date\"],\n","        subset[\"cases_ma7\"],\n","        label=level\n","    )\n","\n","plt.title(\n","    \"Risk Classification Timeline\"\n",")\n","\n","plt.xlabel(\"Date\")\n","plt.ylabel(\"7-Day Moving Average Cases\")\n","\n","plt.legend()\n","\n","plt.grid(True)\n","\n","plt.show()"],"metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/","height":718},"id":"5MGZ7AsxuBVy","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1787322490800,"user_tz":0,"elapsed":950,"user":{"displayName":"Clement Kofi Okyere Biew","userId":"06693515639474326220"}},"outputId":"0dc207a7-0844-4af6-b1b2-1f96350b4427"},"execution_count":20,"outputs":[{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":["<Figure size 1600x800 with 1 Axes>"],"image/png":"\n"},"metadata":{}}]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["# Interpretation of Risk Timeline\n","\n","The risk timeline provides a visual representation of outbreak intensity throughout the study period.\n","\n","Several transitions between risk states can be observed:\n","\n","- Early observations were predominantly classified as low-risk and moderate-risk.\n","- Increasing transmission activity during May, June, and July resulted in more frequent high-risk classifications.\n","- Critical-risk periods were concentrated during major outbreak waves and represented a relatively small proportion of total observations.\n","- Following the outbreak peak, risk levels gradually shifted back toward lower categories.\n","\n","The classification framework successfully differentiated routine transmission activity from periods of elevated and unusually high outbreak intensity."],"metadata":{"id":"SGq1iAeMui4n"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["# Key Findings\n","\n","The statistical surveillance framework produced several important findings:\n","\n","- A rolling monitoring approach successfully adapted to changing outbreak conditions throughout the study period.\n","- Statistical warning and alert thresholds responded dynamically to local transmission patterns.\n","- Outbreak activity was distributed across four surveillance categories, indicating meaningful variation in transmission intensity.\n","- Low-risk days accounted for 42.11% of classified observations.\n","- Moderate-risk days accounted for 18.71% of classified observations.\n","- High-risk days accounted for 30.99% of classified observations.\n","- Critical-risk days accounted for 8.19% of classified observations.\n","- The highest levels of outbreak activity occurred during July and August 2020.\n","- The surveillance framework was able to identify periods of elevated transmission while maintaining interpretable statistical decision rules.\n","\n","These findings demonstrate the usefulness of adaptive statistical monitoring for outbreak surveillance and early warning detection."],"metadata":{"id":"Cap2hEuJuzZA"}},{"cell_type":"code","source":[],"metadata":{"id":"qxl88LoWuNl4"},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[]}]}